The publish gate. While this file exists the release workflow tags nothing.

yze-md-docfiles is not published yet, and every push while it was unheld minted
a version: v0.1.0 and v0.1.1 both point at trees carrying defects an adversarial
review has since found and repaired. Those tags cost nothing today only because
the repository is private and proxy.golang.org has never been asked for this
module — the first fetch after it goes public would cache whichever tree it
lands on, permanently, and sum.golang.org would record its hash forever.

So the hold stays until publication is a decision rather than a side effect of a
push: the leak vet passes over the whole tree and its full history, an
adversarial round returns clean, the stale tags are deleted, and only then is a
single v0.1.0 cut deliberately from a tree somebody chose.

Removing this file IS the act of publishing. Do not remove it to quiet a
workflow.
